{:edb/db-before-t 1354 :edb/db-after-t 1355 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534667 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:43:40.113Z" 13194139534667 true] [17592186171767 1100 "Which of the following functions has the codomain $[0,1]$?\n\n1. $p: \\{0, 1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\n2. $q: \\mathbb{R} \\to [0, 1]$\n3. $[MATH: r: [0,1] \\to [0, 1)]$" 13194139534667 false] [17592186171767 1100 "Which of the following functions has the codomain $[0,1]?$\n\n- $p: \\{ 0, 1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\n\n- $q: \\mathbb{R} \\to [ 0, 1 ]$\n\n- $r: [0,1] \\to [ 0, 1 )$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186171767 1145 "The notation $f: X \\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y$. In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X$,\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $\\mathbb{R}$, the set of real numbers.\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[0, 1]$, the interval from $0$ and $1$ (including $0$ and $1$).\n- The codomain of $r$ is $[MATH: [0, 1),]$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (including $0$ but not including $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534667 false] [17592186171767 1145 "The notation $f: X \\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $\\mathbb{R},$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[ 0, 1 ],$ the interval from $0$ and $1$ (including $0$ and $1$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $[ 0, 1),$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (including $0$ but not including $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534667 true] [17592186171768 1100 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n$\\qquad$ *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$.\"*\n\n- $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\n- $g: Y \\to \\mathbb{Q}$\n\n- $g:\\mathbb{R} \\to Y$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186171768 1100 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n$\\qquad$ *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$.\"*\n\n1. $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n2. $g: Y \\to \\mathbb{Q}$\n3. $g:\\mathbb{R} \\to Y$" 13194139534667 false] [17592186171768 1145 "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $\\mathbb Q$, and the codomain of $g$ is $Y$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139534667 false] [17592186171768 1145 "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $\\mathbb Q,$ and the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139534667 true] [17592186171769 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to $g(x)=x-x^3$?\n\n1. $g:x \\mapsto x-x^3$\n2. $g:x \\mapsto -x^3$\n3. $g:-x \\mapsto x^3$" 13194139534667 false] [17592186171769 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to $g(x)=x-x^3?$\n\n- $g:x \\mapsto x-x^3$\n\n- $g:x \\mapsto -x^3$\n\n- $g:-x \\mapsto x^3$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186171769 1145 "The notation $g(x)=x-x^3$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $x-x^3$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng:x \\mapsto x-x^3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534667 false] [17592186171769 1145 "The notation $g(x)=x-x^3$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $x-x^3$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng:x \\mapsto x-x^3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534667 true] [17592186171770 1100 "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g: \\{ -1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}?$\n\n- The domain of $g$ is $\\{ -1,0,1 \\}$\n\n- The codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$\n\n- The range of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186171770 1100 "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g: \\{-1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}$?\n\n1. The domain of $g$ is $\\{-1,0,1 \\}$\n2. The codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$\n3. The range of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$" 13194139534667 false] [17592186171770 1145 "The notation\n\n$$\ng: \\{-1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $\\{-1,0,1 \\}$ to the set $\\mathbb{R}$. In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $\\{-1,0,1 \\}$, and\n- the codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$. Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534667 false] [17592186171770 1145 "The notation \n\n$$\ng: \\{ -1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $\\{ -1,0,1 \\}$ to the set $\\mathbb{R}.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $\\{ -1,0,1 \\},$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534667 true] [17592186171961 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302276 13194139534667 true] [17592186171961 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302283 13194139534667 true] [17592186171961 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302332 13194139534667 true] [17592186171961 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302339 13194139534667 true] [17592186171961 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302346 13194139534667 true] [17592186171962 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302290 13194139534667 true] [17592186171962 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302353 13194139534667 true] [17592186171962 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302360 13194139534667 true] [17592186171962 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302367 13194139534667 true] [17592186171963 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302297 13194139534667 true] [17592186171963 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302304 13194139534667 true] [17592186171963 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302374 13194139534667 true] [17592186171964 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302311 13194139534667 true] [17592186171964 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302318 13194139534667 true] [17592186171964 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302325 13194139534667 true] [17592186171964 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302381 13194139534667 true] [17592186171964 1020 #edb/ref 17592186302388 13194139534667 true] [17592186172554 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534667 true] [17592186172554 1100 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set of real numbers.\"*" 13194139534667 true] [17592186172554 1100 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n> *\"The function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set of real numbers.\"*" 13194139534667 false] [17592186172554 1145 "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set of real numbers\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $g:X\\to R$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $X,$ and the codomain of $g$ is $R.$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186172555 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534667 true] [17592186172555 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to $f: x ↦ x^{2} - 3$?" 13194139534667 false] [17592186172555 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to $f:x↦{x}^{2}-3?$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186172555 1145 "The notation $f:x↦{x}^{2}-3$ means that the function $f$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to ${x}^{2}-3$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}-3.\n$$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186172556 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534667 true] [17592186172556 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to $h(x) = 5x + x^{2}$?" 13194139534667 false] [17592186172556 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to $h(x)=5x+{x}^{2}?$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186172556 1145 "The notation $h(x)=5x+{x}^{2}$ means that the function $h$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $5x+{x}^{2}$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\nh:x↦5x+{x}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302276 1017 #edb/ref 17592186302277 13194139534667 true] [17592186302276 1089 "q-104778" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302276 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534667 true] [17592186302276 1100 "Which of the following functions has the codomain ${0,1}?$\n\n- $p:{0,1}\\to Z$\n- $q:[0,1]\\to {0,1}$\n- $r:{0,1}\\to (0,1)$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302276 1113 #uuid "0f04f32d-b52c-5a8d-8938-51184b8d7e95" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302276 1145 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $Z,$ the set of integers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is ${0,1},$ the set containing the two numbers $0$ and $1$ only.\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $(0,1),$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (excluding both $0$ and $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302278 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302279 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302280 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302281 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302282 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1041 "selection" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302282 13194139534667 true] [17592186302277 1110 #uuid "6611876c-4df0-5aa8-80a6-e2e64a557ce0" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302278 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534667 true] [17592186302278 1111 #uuid "a4128809-363c-51c1-8592-9f3936fee831" 13194139534667 true] [1759