ram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $g$ is ${0,1,2}$\n- The codomain of $g$ is ${-1,0,1,2}$\n- The range of $g$ is ${0,1,2}$" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302325 1113 #uuid "44c659b0-02a0-5558-84be-8148a9610549" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302325 1145 "The notation $g:X\\to Y$ means that the function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $g$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X={-1,0,1,2},$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y={0,1,2},$\n\n- the range of $g$ is ${0,1,2},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"III only.\"" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302327 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302328 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302329 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302330 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302331 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1041 "selection" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302329 13194139534667 true] [17592186302326 1110 #uuid "0db130e5-b590-5d33-b222-c1521597c1f4" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302327 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534667 true] [17592186302327 1111 #uuid "d9377612-74f1-536a-918e-4f4b46a21318" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302328 1034 "I only" 13194139534667 true] [17592186302328 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534667 true] [17592186302328 1111 #uuid "c9e18915-94d8-59b8-89e4-e2d79544abdd" 13194139534667 tr